  "_comment": "Global escape table for the proxy alphabet. Proxy writes any orthography in plain a-z and reads back exactly, without a per-language table: an a-z letter stands for itself, a literal x doubles to xx, and anything else is written x<payload>x -- ɔ is xox, ŋ is xngx, a combining acute is xqx. Reading back is a scan, so the code cannot be misread and no language can fail. Payloads start from the universal spelling of the letter so an escape stays legible, and take a suffix only where two letters would collide.",
